.TH NPP 1 "2026-09-04" "1.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
npp \- Nextpad++ terminal editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B npp
.RI [ FILE ...]
.br
.B npp \-
.br
.B npp \-g
.RI [ FILE ...]
.br
.B npp \-\-cmd config
.RB { show | paths }
.br
.B npp \-\-list\-commands
.br
.B npp \-\-version
|
.B \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B npp
is the terminal face of Nextpad++: the same Scintilla/Lexilla engine, the
same syntax highlighting (built-in languages and User Defined Languages),
the same themes, and the same settings directory as the graphical
.BR nextpad-plus-plus (1),
rendered as cells in a terminal so it works over SSH and inside tmux.
It shares nothing with the GUI at run time except files: themes,
langs, UDLs, function-list parsers and
.I config.xml
are read from the common settings directory, and editor preferences
(tab width, word wrap, indent guides, whitespace/EOL display, edge column,
the active theme) are mirrored live whenever the GUI saves them.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I FILE ...
Open the files. A trailing
.BI : LINE [: COL ]
positions the caret; classic
.BI \-n LINE
and
.BI \-c COL
flags are accepted as well.
.TP
.B \-
Read the initial buffer from standard input.
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-gui
Hand the files to the graphical Nextpad++ instead (no effect over SSH).
.TP
.BI \-settingsDir= DIR
Use
.I DIR
as the settings directory instead of the default.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-commands
Print the command table (name and key binding) and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-cmd config show
Print the resolved configuration; 
.B \-\-cmd config paths
prints the directories in use.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B ^P
Command palette (fuzzy search over every command).
.TP
.B F10
Menu bar (File, Edit, Search, View, Encoding, Language).
.TP
.B ^L
Buffers list; 
.B F1
key-bindings card.
.TP
.BR ^S ", " ^Q
Save; quit. Unsaved changes survive a quit (hot exit) and are restored on
the next launch.
.TP
.BR ^C ", " ^X ", " ^V
Copy, cut, paste. Copies go to the terminal via OSC 52 (works over SSH in
kitty, foot, WezTerm, Ghostty and others); locally
.BR wl-copy / wl-paste
or
.B xclip
are used when present.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NPP_TUI_COLOR_MODE
Force
.BR truecolor ", " 256 " or " 16
colours instead of detecting from
.BR COLORTERM / TERM .
.TP
.B NPP_TUI_THEME
Path of a stylers.xml to use instead of the GUI's active theme.
.TP
.B NPP_TUI_GUI_CONFIG
Path of the GUI
.I config.xml
to mirror (default: the shared settings directory).
.TP
.B NPP_TUI_NO_CLIPBOARD
Disable the system clipboard bridge (OSC 52 and local tools).
.SH REMOTE USE
Run
.B ssh \-t host npp FILE
for a one-shot session. Set
.B TERM=xterm-256color
if the remote terminfo lacks your terminal's entry, and forward
.B COLORTERM
(ssh
.BR SendEnv / AcceptEnv )
for truecolor. Inside tmux truecolor needs tmux's own RGB passthrough.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/nextpad++/config.xml
GUI preferences, mirrored live.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/nextpad++/tui-session.xml
The terminal editor's own session (never shared with the GUI).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nextpad-plus-plus (1)
